Structural Check
- [S1] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v1 = 'available'` on `b1 -> n4` uses undefined variable `v1`. | Guard `v1 = 'not_available'` on `b1 -> n6` uses undefined variable `v1`. | DSL: guard(b1,n4,"v1 = 'available'"); guard(b1,n6,"v1 = 'not_available'")

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v1 = 'available'` on `b1 -> n4` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Guard `v1 = 'not_available'` on `b1 -> n6` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b1,n4,"v1 = 'available'"); guard(b1,n6,"v1 = 'not_available'")
- [L2] LSC2 failed: Guards outgoing from an XOR branch must be mutually exclusive. | Branch `b1` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range.
- [L3] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b1` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range.
